\section{Experiments}\label{sec:experiments}

\paragraph{Data and protocol.}
Table~\ref{tab:data} lists the \nSets{} datasets: the Arena-55k crowd votes (64 models) and their single-turn subset; \nJudges{} LLM judges that re-labelled the \emph{same} single-turn battles (verdict from position-averaged probabilities, ties as the judge returns them); MT-Bench expert and GPT-4 judgments of the same questions and answer pairs, GPT-4 also restricted to the pairs the experts judged; and \nNBA{} NBA regular seasons (franchises, game outcomes, no ties). We compute $k^{*}$ for \emph{all} $M(M-1)/2$ pairs of every dataset and both alteration families (\nConclusions{} conclusions per family), with $B=\nBootCore$ cluster bootstrap resamples (Section~\ref{sec:method}) and the same-graph null from 20 replicates on 300 $z$-stratified pairs per dataset. Aggregate statements are limited to $z\in[1,8]$; the margin $\pm\deltaMargin$ comes from synthetic calibration (Appendix~\ref{app:synth}); Appendix~\ref{app:repro} gives the order of the analysis plan and the results.

