\subsection{A confidence interval does not make a ranking robust}\label{sec:survival}
A pair is \emph{separated} when the 95\% bootstrap intervals of the two models do not overlap, the published view. Figure~\ref{fig:survival} follows how many of these pairs remain separated as the adversary's budget grows, in absolute terms and in standard-error units. Against a targeted change, half of the separated pairs are lost at about \halfCrowdDelPct\% of $N$ in the Arena crowd data (\halfCrowdFlipPct\% for outcome flips) and at \halfJudgeDelPct\% and \halfJudgeFlipPct\% for the LLM judges, against \halfSportsDelPct\% and \halfSportsFlipPct\% for the NBA seasons and \halfExpertDelPct\% and \halfExpertFlipPct\% for MT-Bench expert labels (median over \nSurvCrowd{}, \nSurvJudge{}, \nSurvSports{} and \nSurvExpert{} datasets). In standard-error units the same budgets are \halfCrowdDelSe{}, \halfJudgeDelSe{} and \halfExpertDelSe{} for deletion (\halfCrowdFlipSe{}, \halfJudgeFlipSe{} and \halfExpertFlipSe{} for flips) in the crowd, judge and expert data, and \halfSportsDelSe{} (flips: \halfSportsFlipSe{}) for the NBA seasons: the common scale removes most of the difference between the designs, but not that of the NBA seasons, which we do not explain. Random alteration does not do this: up to \randBudgetMax\% of $N$ deleted or flipped at random, no design drops below \randSurvMin{} separated. At the size of the smallest adversarial change that reverses a conclusion, a random change of the same size reverses \randAtKDel\% (deletion) or \randAtKFlip\% (flip) of the conclusions (Table~\ref{tab:search}). For deletion at the budget $k^{*}$ itself, none of 300 random draws reversed any sampled pair with $z\in[1,8]$ in any design (rule of three: below $3\times10^{-4}$ for Arena to $2\times10^{-3}$ for MT-Bench), as the formula predicts; flips were not measured this way. The adversary therefore works at a budget where noise has essentially no effect, and the ratio between the two budgets is a lower bound, not a value: by the formula, whose accuracy is checked on synthetic data (Appendix~\ref{app:synth}), the fraction of random deletions at which the reversal probability reaches 16\% is at least \fqOverAdvMinSports{} (NBA), \fqOverAdvMinExpert{} (MT-Bench expert and LLM judges) and \fqOverAdvMinCrowd{} (Arena crowd) times the adversary's fraction $k^{*}/N$, over the sampled pairs. The intervals in Figure~\ref{fig:survival} treat pairs as independent and are optimistic.

